'''Alessandria''' ({{lang-bl|Lissandria}}; {{Langx|tpk|Maranduba|4=place of fish nets}}) is the most populous city within the [[Hesperia|Hesperian community]], and the [[List of cities in Balisca by population|third most populous]] in [[Balisca]] overall. The [[Metropolitan City of Alessandria|wider metropolitan area]] comprising the neighboring communes is the third-largest in Balisca, with a population of around 11 million people. The metropolitan region forms the majority of the Baliscan portion of the [[Augusta Corridor|Alessandria–Otranto metropolitan region]], a [[w:Transborder agglomeration|transborder agglomeration]] which with a population upwards of 13 million, making it one of the world's largest. The [[Port of Alessandria]] is the [[List of busiest ports in Adonia|? busiest port in Abyala]] and the ? busiest container port on the [[Aethiopian Ocean]]. The city is ranked as an [[Adonia Globalization and World Cities Ranks|Alpha]] [[w:global city|global city]] in the [[Adonia Globalization and World Cities Ranks|Globalization and World Cities Research Network]].

Historically, Alessandria and its surrounding area constituted the primary gateway for [[immigration to Balisca|immigrants coming to Balisca]]. As many as 400 languages are spoken in Alessandria, making it one of the most linguistically diverse cities in the world. Alessandria is home to more than 2.4 million residents born outside of Balisca, the third-largest foreign-born population of any Baliscan city. It is known for its eclectic [[Alessandria#Architecture|architecture]] reflective of its rich cultural background. It is a [[W:Multiculturalism|multicultural]] city that is home to over 200 ethnic and religious groups, contributing to its culture as well as to the [[Alessandrian dialect|dialect]] (popularly known as ''vesperiano'') spoken in the city and it's [[W:Hinterland|hinterland]].

Alessandria traces its origins to an trading outpost founded by {{W|Republic of Noli|Nolani sailors}} in 1624. It rapidly grew as it received thousands of expelled Spaniards, mostly [[W:Moriscos|Moriscos]], [[Mozbayana|Mozbayán]] and [[W:Sephardic Jews|Sephardic Jews]]. By the dawn of the 18th century, Alessandria was amongst the most successful Mesogean outposts in Balisca, and a major trade post of the [[Hesperian League]]. It went on to become the preeminent political, artistic and business center in Abyala during the [[Volisanya Boba]] period.

